\subsection{Selecting a language}
\label{sec:setup-language}

The first positional argument of [[init]] picks a language
toolchain.  The enum below currently has only one member,
but the point of using an enum (rather than a plain string)
is that Typer uses enum members as valid CLI choices
automatically, so adding [[java]] or [[cpp]] later becomes
a one-line change with no CLI-surface churn.
Subclassing [[str]] makes Typer render the values as plain
words in [[--help]] and lets the enum compare equal to
ordinary strings in tests.

<<constants>>=
class Language(str, enum.Enum):
    """Supported student-language toolchains.

    Used as the positional argument of ``learnlog init``.
    New members become new valid CLI choices automatically
    via Typer's built-in enum support.
    """

    python = "python"
