@

The tag boundaries are read only when a boundary was given, exactly
as the metrics resolver does (\cref{sec:metrics-command}): they cost
two more Git calls, and a plain [[learnlog list]] must stay at the
constant number the test at the end of this section pins.

\paragraph{The window.}
A listing's windows are the report's windows read by a different kind
of reader, so the vocabulary is the same one and the boundary
resolution is literally the same function.
Two things differ, and both follow from a listing being a listing.
[[all]] is not a window here but the absence of one: a report's
[[all]] starts at the first run because a report has to name the span
it measured, while a listing has nothing to name and a window would
quietly drop the records whose start time cannot be read---the
opposite of what a listing is for.
And a [[--until]] with no [[--since]] leaves the lower bound open
instead of closing it at the present moment, because
[[explicit_window]] defaults a missing [[--since]] to the first
\emph{record}, and with no record list to ask it would answer
[[now]]---an empty window for every listing of the past.

<<helper functions>>=
def refuse_two_windows(period, since, until):
    """Exit when ``--period`` is given beside ``--since``/``--until``."""
    if period is not None and (since or until):
        raise SystemExit(
            "--period cannot be combined with --since or --until."
        )


def list_window(period, since, until, starts, now=None):
    """The ``[start, end)`` a listing covers, or ``None`` for none.

    ``starts`` maps tag names to their period starts, for a
    boundary that names a tag.  A missing boundary is left open
    rather than closed at the present moment.
    """
    if since or until:
        try:
            begin = (
                resolve_boundary(since, starts) if since
                else datetime.datetime.min
            )
            end = (
                resolve_boundary(until, starts, inclusive_end=True)
                if until else datetime.datetime.max
            )
        except ValueError as error:
            raise SystemExit(str(error)) from error
        return begin, end
    if period is None or period is Period.ALL:
        return None
    return period_window(period, [], now)
