When at least one outcome flag is active (so [[wanted]] is
non-empty), we intersect it with the commit's outcomes
(\cref{sec:commit-outcomes}) and skip the commit if the
intersection is empty.  Set intersection gives exactly the
semantics we want: each flag contributes one outcome to
[[wanted]], passing both flags matches any commit with at least
one finalized run, and the [[unknown]] outcome from unfinalized
runs never matches because we never add it to [[wanted]].

