\paragraph{The file filters.}
Which files a record ran and changed is read by the commit readers
(\cref{sec:record-files}).
Those readers make both answers paths relative to the project root.
The changed files cost one more Git call, for the whole log.
Like the tag boundaries, it is made only when a file filter was
given, so a plain [[learnlog list]] keeps its constant count.
The set of every path the log has seen, [[known]], lets a script
recorded by its absolute path be placed in a log cloned from
elsewhere (\cref{sec:record-files}).

