The skip comes right after the tag names are read, before the
message is merged and filtered, because the tag map is already in
memory and an untagged record needs no more work.
Filtering tags adds no Git call: the map was read for the
[[(tag: ...)]] markers anyway.
[[--all]] is not needed to reach a tag on a review run, since a tagged
record is never hidden (\cref{sec:visible-commits}).
That matters for a lecture's bundle recorded by an older learnlog,
which put a bare [[learnlog tag]] on HEAD, and so on the
[[learnlog list]] the lecturer had typed just before tagging.

One tag stays out of reach.
A tag on the log's initial commit has no run to summarise, and the
listing skips records without a summary.
Only a [[learnlog tag]] typed before the first run of any kind puts a
tag there.
[[learnlog init]]'s own install is already a run.

