Let's verify the outcome filters.  The first two tests use a
two-commit sequence---one successful commit and one failed
commit---to check each flag in isolation.  The third confirms
that passing both flags combines them by union, not
intersection (any finalized run matches).  The fourth is the
headline test for the student recovery workflow: a single
commit containing one successful and one failed run must appear
under \emph{both} flags, so the student's most recent working
state is not hidden by a later re-run that broke it.

