@

The tests that follow all need the same two-machine situation---one
log, pushed to a remote, cloned back into a second directory---so we
build it once.
The clone's work tree starts empty, which is what [[clone]] leaves
behind (\cref{sec:clone}); the student's files in it are the ones the
test writes.
A cloned repository has never been through [[init_repo]], so it lacks
the settings that make committing work regardless of the developer's
global Git configuration; the tests below record runs in the clone, so
the helper applies the one that matters.

<<test functions>>=
def _two_machine_log(workdir, runner, monkeypatch):
    """Push a log to a bare remote and clone it back.

    Returns the clone's directory.
    """
