A branch whose tip cannot be read is the last state left, and no
repository a command can construct exhibits it---construction heals
an unborn branch with the initial commit before [[pull]] runs.
So the test manufactures the failing probe itself: it lets every
Git call through except the one reading the local tip, which is
made to fail the way it does in a damaged repository.

