Hidden means absent from the catalogue and nothing more, so the test
asks both halves: the help output must not advertise the command, and
the command must still answer to its name.
The help is checked against the word as a command entry rather than
as a substring, because \enquote{git} appears in other commands' help
texts legitimately.
Typer draws its command table with the box-drawing character U+2502,
and the test needs that exact character to recognise a table row---but
noweave copies code chunks verbatim into the woven \LaTeX{}, where
pdf\LaTeX{} has no glyph set up for it and stops with an error.
Spelling it [[chr(0x2502)]] gives the running test the real character
while the source stays within what the document engine typesets:

