\subsection{The [[checkout]] command}
\label{sec:checkout}

[[learnlog list --success]] ends with the hash of the last version
that worked, and the question a student asks next is how to get it
back.
The answer used to be the escape hatch,
[[learnlog git checkout <hash>]], and it has two problems that are
really one.
Git's checkout moves [[HEAD]] onto the commit, so the student ends up
detached: the runs they record afterwards still reach the branch
(\cref{sec:recording-branch}), but [[git status]] says
[[HEAD detached]], the log they see from there is the old one, and
nothing tells them how to get back.
And it refuses when a modified file would be overwritten, which is
the right instinct---those edits are in no commit---and the wrong
outcome, since the student has no way to commit them except to run
the program they are trying to abandon.

[[learnlog checkout <run>]] answers both by doing one thing first: it
records the files as they are, as an ordinary run record whose header
is a snapshot of the work tree, and only then restores the earlier
tree (\cref{sec:restore-code-state}) and closes the record with a
trailer that carries the restored tree.
The snapshot is what makes the overwrite safe---every file about to
be replaced is in the log before it goes---and it is why this command
may overwrite without asking where the passthrough refuses.
[[HEAD]] never leaves the branch, so the restored files are simply
the next version the log commits: the branch tip's tree \emph{is} the
restored tree, [[git status]] is clean, and the next run's diff is
the student's own editing rather than the reversion.
The record is written by the command, not by the autostart that
records [[play]] and [[list]] (\cref{sec:veto}), because the command
has to know the snapshot exists before it touches a file, and because
a mistyped hash must not leave a record of a checkout that never
happened.
Two same-named commands with different manners are a trap, so the
difference is stated once, plainly: the passthrough is safe by
refusal and leaves the student detached; this command is safe by
snapshot and keeps them on the branch.

<<typer commands>>=
