The command has grown two more shapes since the one above, and they
are told apart before anything is read.
[[learnlog checkout --from lecture.learnlog <hash>]] copies a run's
files in from another log (\cref{sec:checkout-from}), and
[[learnlog checkout --restore]] undoes a checkout
(\cref{sec:checkout-restore}).
Each option belongs to one shape: [[--output]] names where the copied
files go, so it needs [[--from]]; [[--restore]] chooses among this
log's own checkouts, so it takes neither.
A destination outside the project is refused for the reason that
makes the copy worth recording at all: files there are in no
snapshot, and the log would say the student got files it cannot
show.
The Git directory is inside the project but is not the student's
files, so it is refused with the same words.
Without [[--output]] the copy goes into a directory named after the
source---[[lecture21/]] for [[lecture21.learnlog]]---so that a
student who fetches from several lectures gets one folder each and
never a lecture's [[main.py]] over their own; [[-o .]] asks for the
project root explicitly.
The name is the source's last path component with the export suffix
gone, which serves a bundle, a ProgSnap2 archive and a directory
alike.

