Let's verify the chooser on a history with two checkouts and edits
between them.
Answering [[2]] brings back the files from before the older one; the
restore is then itself the newest checkout, so [[--restore 1]] brings
back the files from before the restore, edit included; and the branch
only ever grows---every commit it had is still there, in order, with
the restore's two on top.

