When [[batch]] is [[None]] (the user did not pass [[-b]]),
we fall back to TTY detection via [[sys.stdout.isatty()]].
An explicit [[--batch]] or [[--no-batch]] always wins.

<<choose playback mode>>=
use_batch = (
    batch if batch is not None
    else not sys.stdout.isatty()
)
if use_batch:
    if start_index is None:
        start_index = 0
    play_batch(repo, records, start_index, show_all,
               trailers=scan.trailers, tag_map=tag_map,
               raw=raw, color=color)
else:
    if start_index is None:
        start_index = len(records) - 1
    viewer = PlaybackViewer(
        repo, records, start_index, show_all,
        trailers=scan.trailers, tag_map=tag_map,
        raw=raw, color=color,
    )
    viewer.run()
@

The scan and the tag map are read here once and handed to both media,
which otherwise read each lazily on their own; thinning the list costs
no Git call the viewer was not already going to make.

A live [[.learnlog/]] can never thin to nothing, because its initial
commit has no run block and is therefore never hidden.
A ProgSnap2 source can: the reconstruction starts its branch over
from the dataset (\cref{progsnap2}), so a dataset holding only
review runs rebuilds into a log in which every commit is hidden.
The viewer would open on index [[-1]] of an empty list, so the case
is refused before either medium is chosen, with the flag that would
show something.

