Colour is the one behaviour the runner can only half exercise, so the
three assertions below are chosen for what a TTY-less process
\emph{can} decide.
Without a terminal the automatic rule says no colour, so the default
invocation must be free of escapes; [[--color]] must overrule the
missing terminal; and [[NO_COLOR]] must not overrule [[--color]], which
is the half of the [[NO_COLOR]] convention that tools get wrong.
The escape we look for is the green of an added diff line, which is
the first colour a student sees.

