The bookmark goes through the same lookup as a starting ref, so it
gets the same three answers: an index into the shown list; the refusal
naming [[--all]] when the record last viewed is one playback hides,
which happens when the previous playback ran under [[--all]] and
stopped on a review run; and a message of its own when the hash is in
no record at all.
The last case is real rather than defensive: a ProgSnap2
reconstruction gives its commits new hashes (\cref{progsnap2}), so a
trace exported from one log names records that the rebuilt log does
not have.
A log with no playback in it has nothing to continue, and a starting
ref beside the flag is two answers to one question, refused rather
than ranked.
Which log the bookmark is read from is the question the rest of this
part answers.

The source a playback was given is on its recorded command line, and
[[source_arguments]] (\cref{sec:source-files}) reads it back from the
words of the [[Arguments:]] field, which [[parse_run_arguments]]
restores exactly as typed.
A recorded [[-f]] value and one typed now are compared as resolved
paths: the typed one against the current directory, the recorded one
against the directory its run was started in, which the header names
relative to the project root (\cref{sec:run-directory}).
So a lecture played from a subfolder as [[-f ../lecture.learnlog]]
and continued from the root as [[-f lecture.learnlog]] are the same
lecture.
A header from before the directory was recorded has no better answer
than the current directory, and a mismatch there costs at most a
\enquote{nothing to continue}, never a wrong record.
No [[-f]] means the project's own log, so a playback without one and
[[-f .]] name the same log and match.

<<helper functions>>=
def playback_source_argument(run):
    """The ``-f``/``--from`` value a recorded playback was given.

    ``None`` when the playback showed the project's own log.
    """
    values = source_arguments(
        parse_run_arguments(run["arguments"] or "")
    )
    return values[-1] if values else None


def source_path(value, own, directory=None):
    """The log ``value`` names, resolved; the project's own for ``None``.

    A relative ``value`` is taken from ``directory``, a path relative
    to ``own``, when given, and from the current directory otherwise.
    """
    if value is None:
        return pathlib.Path(own).resolve()
    base = pathlib.Path.cwd() if directory is None \
        else pathlib.Path(own) / directory
    return (base / value).resolve()
@

The bookmark is found before the source is resolved, because it may
\emph{be} the source: when no [[-f]] was given, the playback found
decides what is played.
A source that has gone since---a bundle the student deleted---is
refused by name rather than left to the resolver's generic complaint,
since the student did not type it this time and would not know what
it refers to.
The source handed on is the resolved path, since the recorded words
were relative to where they were typed, and the name shown is that
path relative to here, the way the student would type it now.

<<find the playback to continue>>=
own = find_learnlog_dir()
if own is None:
    raise SystemExit(NOTHING_TO_CONTINUE_NOTE)
own_repo = LearnlogRepo(own)
wanted = None if source is None else source_path(source, own)
playback = last_playback(
    get_commits(own_repo), scan_run_commits(own_repo),
    matches=None if wanted is None else (
        lambda run: source_path(
            playback_source_argument(run), own, run["directory"],
        ) == wanted
    ),
)
if playback is None:
    if source is None:
        raise SystemExit(NOTHING_TO_CONTINUE_NOTE)
    raise SystemExit(
        f"Nothing to continue: you have not played {source} yet."
    )
viewed = playback["viewed"][-1][0]
if source is None:
    recorded = playback_source_argument(playback)
    if recorded is not None:
        played = source_path(recorded, own, playback["directory"])
        shown = os.path.relpath(played)
        if not played.exists():
            raise SystemExit(
                f"Cannot continue: {shown}, which you were "
                "playing, is not here any more."
            )
        source = str(played)
        typer.echo(
            f"Continuing {shown} where you left off.", err=True,
        )
