\subsection{The [[metrics]] command group}
\label{sec:metrics-command}

[[learnlog metrics]] is one pipeline with five views
(\cref{metrics}): [[time]], [[eq]], [[code]] and [[lint]] each
render one family of metrics, and [[trends]] joins them over time.
A Typer sub-application gives the five a common prefix and a common
help page; it is mounted on [[app]] the way pytorial mounts
[[tutorial]] (\cref{sec:tutorial}), except that here the commands are
our own.

<<typer commands>>=
metrics_app = typer.Typer(
    name="metrics",
    help=(
        "Summarise your own development log: time, errors, "
        "code, and how they change."
    ),
    no_args_is_help=True,
)
app.add_typer(metrics_app, name="metrics")
@

The five commands take the same options, so the options are defined
once and each command lists them.
Typer has no option groups; declaring the [[Option]] objects as
constants and naming them in each signature is the nearest thing, and
it keeps the help texts in one place.

