The inputs remember whether a granularity was asked for, because that
is the fact that decides which code to measure; the bucket list alone
cannot say, since a series of one week and a single window both have
one bucket.

Each command is the same handful of lines around a different
[[compute_*]] call, so their signatures are one shared chunk.
An empty series says so and stops; an empty window still prints its
one row, because dashes and zeros in a labelled row are the answer to
\enquote{what did I do this week}.

